  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1018 AM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nWhile we're looking at one more day of record-breaking warmth\ntoday, many spots are likely to wake up to frost Sunday morning, \nmainly along the Cumberland Plateau and other traditional \"cool \nspots\" around the area. High pressure will continue to dominate \nthe weather across Middle Tennessee well into next week.\nTemperatures will warm up gradually after this weekend, but we\ndon't expect to stray too far above seasonal norms even by the\nend of the week. Meanwhile, after Friday, there are no more\nweather-producing systems coming our way any time soon. Therefore,\nthe worsening drought conditions that we are experiencing will\ncontinue to worsen, at least in the near-term.",
